const siteMd=`# Site records\n\nStatus: **PRELIMINARY DESKTOP RECORDS — FIELD CONFIRMATION REQUIRED**\n\n## SITE-N01 — Normal Crossing candidate\n\n- **Coordinate:** 3.1279214, 101.7538643 (**OWNER-PROVIDED**)\n- **Images:** \`screenshots/EVID-SITE-N01-IMG-01.png\`, \`screenshots/EVID-SITE-N01-IMG-02.png\`. Image 2 visibly states May 2024; Image 1 capture date is not visible.\n- **Nearby names:** Jalan Pandan Indah 27 and Jalan Bunga Mawar 1 are legible in Image 1; the Image 2 map overlay says Ampang Jaya, Selangor (**OBSERVED IN SOURCE**). This does not verify jurisdiction.\n- **Visual observation:** divided urban road context, landscaped median/refuge features, yellow crossing/keep-clear-type markings, warning/direction signs, trees, accesses, overhead lines and adjacent development.\n- **Hypotheses:** pedestrian desire may cross the divided road and connect nearby residential/access destinations; eastbound/westbound approaches may support a SmartCross concept. These are **ENGINEERING INFERENCE**, not measurements.\n- **Potential constraints:** tree/vehicle occlusion, access and turning movements, median/refuge geometry, utilities, lighting, drainage, mounting and accessible-route continuity.\n- **Unknowns:** current condition, boundary, authority, lane/road dimensions, traffic/speed/queue volumes, controller/assets, utilities, power, network, drainage, accessibility, sightlines and construction access.\n- **Jurisdiction/authority:** **UNVERIFIED — OWNER/AUTHORITY CONFIRMATION REQUIRED**.\n- **Suitability:** preliminary desktop concept study appears possible, medium-low confidence. No fatal constraint is established or ruled out.\n- **Potential design differences:** general-public demand, side-road/access conflicts and median/refuge treatment may differ materially from SITE-S01.\n\n## SITE-S01 — School Crossing candidate\n\n- **Coordinate:** 3.212429703327789, 101.75199696106526 (**OWNER-PROVIDED**)\n- **Images:** \`screenshots/EVID-SITE-S01-IMG-01.png\`, \`screenshots/EVID-SITE-S01-IMG-02.png\`. May 2024 imagery indicators are visible.\n- **Nearby names:** Jalan Taman Melawati and SK Taman Melawati 2 are legible; a map inset references the Zoo Negara vicinity (**OBSERVED IN SOURCE**). School participation and authority are not verified.\n- **Visual observation:** divided multi-lane road, school frontage/lay-by, fence/gate, waiting/footway context, zebra-type and yellow school/traffic-calming markings, signal heads, median fencing, lighting poles, trees, parked/stopped vehicles and roadside boxes.\n- **Hypotheses:** a strong school-gate-to-opposite-side pedestrian desire line and two directional vehicle approaches may exist. These are **ENGINEERING INFERENCE** until surveyed.\n- **Potential constraints:** arrival/departure parking, door-zone conflict, child visibility, queuing, access movements, median fence continuity, existing controller integration, mature trees, drainage and accessible routes.\n- **Unknowns:** current condition, site/school boundary, authority, school agreement, operating windows, traffic/pupil counts, geometry, controller/assets, utilities, power, network, accessibility and sightlines.\n- **Jurisdiction/authority:** **UNVERIFIED — OWNER/AUTHORITY/SCHOOL CONFIRMATION REQUIRED**.\n- **Suitability:** preliminary desktop concept study appears possible, medium confidence; school-peak operation and existing-signal integration may require redesign. No fatal constraint is established or ruled out.\n- **Potential design differences:** supervised school demand, school-day peaks, child clearance, parking/keep-clear management, lower-speed context and school operating coordination require separate evidence and design.\n\nSee \`site-evidence-checklist.csv\` for the 15 required evidence items per site.\n`;
