const readme=`# SmartCross requirements and drawing-input package\n\n**Status:** PRELIMINARY REQUIREMENTS AND DRAWING-INPUT PACKAGE. NOT AN APPROVED DESIGN, CONSTRUCTION DRAWING, PHYSICAL-HIL RESULT, TENDER-READY BOQ OR APPROVED BOQ BASELINE.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis package extracts and organizes repository and owner-provided evidence for the next design stage for:\n\n- SITE-N01 Normal Crossing candidate: 3.1279214, 101.7538643\n- SITE-S01 School Crossing candidate: 3.212429703327789, 101.75199696106526\n\nIt does not implement or modify traffic-control behavior. Requirements not clearly established are labelled proposed or unresolved.\n\n## Repository baseline\n\n- Path: \`${root}\`\n- Package/repository name: \`lintas-ai-link-2\` / SmartCross application\n- Branch: \`${branch}\`\n- Commit: \`${commit}\`\n- Analysis time: ${generatedAt} (Asia/Kuala_Lumpur)\n- Working tree: **DIRTY**. ${dirtySummary}\n\n## Method\n\nThe analysis inspected repository instructions, package metadata, README, scenario/data contracts, simulation and safety sources, fallback/emergency/heavy-traffic logic, UI, tests, accessibility/governance documents, HIL preparation records, existing BoQ workbooks and the four supplied site images. Facts, owner input, inference and missing evidence use these labels: ${labels}.\n\nThe public simulator URL was attempted through the web retrieval tool and browser-automation command. The web tool reported the URL inaccessible; the \`agent-browser\` command was unavailable. No authentication was bypassed and no live scenario was claimed as observed.\n\n## Key inventory and conflicts\n\n- Modes in source: \`normal\` and \`school\` (\`lib/types.ts\`).\n- Scenario catalogue: one \`<mode>-no-violation\` baseline plus 20 \`<mode>-<slug>\` violation scenarios per mode (42 total in the current simulation source).\n- Seven stages: Approach, Initiation, Detected, Escalation, Conflict, Response and Outcome.\n- Current README states a verified 12-second protected-WALK window; camera fallback code uses a 15-second simulated protected interval, and heavy-traffic UI exposes provisional timing controls. These are separate simulation contexts and must not become field timings without qualified design approval.\n- README/context sources use historic Lintas AI naming while current UI/product metadata use SmartCross.\n- Architecture/context documents may describe proposed dependencies that are not implemented in \`package.json\`; source/package files govern as-built software evidence.\n- Existing BoQ evidence contains a 59-versus-60 item-count discrepancy.\n- Physical-HIL traceability rows are NOT_EXECUTED and do not authorize HIL or field use.\n\n## Package contents\n\n1. \`README.md\` — scope, method, limitations, repository state and review instructions.\n2. \`source-register.csv\` — source inventory and limitations.\n3. \`simulator-evidence-register.csv\` — access attempts and repository-defined scenario evidence.\n4. \`requirements-register.csv\` — 30 candidate requirements with citations, status and verification.\n5. \`site-records.md\` — separate Normal and School desktop records.\n6. \`site-evidence-checklist.csv\` — 15 evidence items for each site.\n7. \`drawing-register.csv\` — per-site and shared drawing/document inputs required from qualified designers.\n8. \`interface-register.csv\` — TBC field interfaces without invented protocols/vendors.\n9. \`requirements-to-design-traceability.csv\` — requirements to evidence, drawings, interfaces and verification.\n10. \`red-team-gap-register.csv\` — preliminary desktop gaps; independent review required.\n11. \`gate-status-and-actions.md\` — ten gates, blockers, owners and next actions.\n12. \`screenshots/\` — preserved copies of the four owner-supplied images with evidence IDs.\n13. \`manifest.sha256\` — SHA-256 hashes for every package file except the manifest itself.\n\n## Limitations and blockers\n\nNo authoritative site nomination/boundary, current survey, measured geometry, traffic counts, controller dossier, utility information, accessibility audit, sightline study, electrical/load design, network architecture, cybersecurity/privacy approval, emergency-agency agreement, controlled design, quotation, formal Red Team closure, authorized physical-HIL result or owner acceptance was supplied. Blank/TBC means unknown, never zero or included.\n\n## Review instructions\n\n1. Review \`source-register.csv\` and confirm the authoritative source/configuration baseline.\n2. Have project-owner and discipline reviewers disposition every proposed/unresolved row in \`requirements-register.csv\`.\n3. Close per-site evidence items independently; do not reuse SITE-N01 geometry/quantities for SITE-S01 or vice versa.\n4. Commission qualified designers to issue the documents in \`drawing-register.csv\`; screenshots are not drawing inputs for measured take-off.\n5. Define and approve interfaces before vendor selection or physical HIL.\n6. Update traceability and close preliminary findings before quantity measurement, pricing or acceptance.\n7. Validate \`manifest.sha256\` after transfer.\n`;
await fs.writeFile(path.join(out,"README.md"),readme,"utf8");

// Manifest last, excluding itself.
async function walk(dir){const outFiles=[];for(const e of await fs.readdir(dir,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(dir,e.name);if(e.isDirectory())outFiles.push(...await walk(p));else outFiles.push(p);}return outFiles;}
const files=(await walk(out)).filter(f=>path.basename(f)!=="manifest.sha256").sort((a,b)=>a.localeCompare(b));
const manifest=[];for(const f of files){const data=await fs.readFile(f);manifest.push(`${crypto.createHash("sha256").update(data).digest("hex")}  ${path.relative(out,f).replaceAll("\\","/")}`);}
await fs.writeFile(path.join(out,"manifest.sha256"),manifest.join("\n")+"\n","utf8");

